# Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

## [1.13.0] - 2026-04-09 - Honesty & Infrastructure (Beta)

### Added

- **Official Linux Deployment Support**: Integrated `run_CraftCommand.sh` and `run_agent.sh` for native POSIX environments.
- **Service Setup Scripts**: Added `systemd` unit templates for Panel and Agent in `scripts/systemd/`.
- **Infrastructure Documentation**: Created `DEPLOYMENT.md` and `LIFECYCLE.md` providing explicit guides for production deployments.
- **Advanced Repair Control**: New UI toggles for **Automatic Repair V3** (System Drift Detection, IO Throttling, Snapshots).
- **Autonomous Patching Engine**: Integrated background update staging (Shadow Staging) with "Last Mile" atomic swap logic in launchers.
- **Data Protection Overlay**: Updates now explicitly skip user directories (`data/`, `minecraft_servers/`, `.env`) during synchronization.

### Improved

- **Technical Terminology Update**: Migrated all references from "Auto-Healing" to **"Automatic Repair"** for technical accuracy.
- **"Anti-Slop" Documentation Overhaul**: Sanitized `README.md` and docs to remove AI-generated marketing jargon in favor of technical transparency.
- **Knowledge Base Consolidation**: Centralized 10 scattered `skill.md` architectural files into a unified repository in `docs/architecture/knowledge/`.
- **UI Density & Focus**: Implemented collapsible "Advanced" settings to fulfill the "Keep UI Clean" requirement while providing power-user control.

### Fixed & Hardened

- **Security Hardening**:
  - **Session Hardening**: Verified 24h JWT expiration, JTI session tracking, and revocation support.
  - **Authentication Security**: Verified Rate Limiting on Login/2FA and robust Path Traversal prevention.
  - **IO Validation**: whitelisted environment keys and dangerous command rejection for spawned processes.
- **Data & Process Integrity**:
  - **Atomic Saves**: Implemented/Verified `temp+rename` patterns for both monolithic and fragmented database writes.
  - **Agent Reliability**: Added exponential backoff and max-restart safety logic to `LocalAgentManager`.
  - **Error Visibility**: Fixed 16 silent error-swallowing catch blocks across core backend services.

## [1.12.5] - 2026-03-26 - Stability & Core Architecture

- **Engine Optimization**: $O(N)$ process tracking, 64KB reverse-buffer log tailing ($O(1)$), and single-root file watching to minimize OS handles.
- **Team Panel & Collaboration**: Integrated high-fidelity chat/activity history, granular presence tracking, and administrative command center.
- **Diagnostics**: 4-tier intelligence pipeline with causality suppression and "Zombie Adoption" for orphaned processes.
- **Infrastructure**: Native **Playit.gg** integration, Docker runtime abstraction, and hardened SHA-256 node handshakes.
- **UI & Minecraft 2026**: Dynamic Mojang/Bedrock manifest fetching and persistent multi-route deployment monitoring.

## [1.12.0] - 2026-03-20 - Operational Excellence

- **Mod Management**: Triple-layer stabilization for Modrinth API, including server-side filtering, dependency resolution, and automated auto-healing for client-only mod conflicts.
- **Infrastructure**: Multi-sequential scheduled tasks, graceful countdown shutdowns, and grid-based topology for node telemetry.
- **Console & Terminal**: 50-item command history, multi-level log filtering, and one-click log exports.
- **UX/UI**: Replaced all native browser alerts with theme-aware dialogs. Integrated proactive pre-boot diagnosis to block startup on known-bad configs.
- **Storage**: High-efficiency batch storage layer for audits/notifications with automated `.env` parity checks.
- **Fixes**: 30+ stability patches covering Java deployment freezes, BDS 404s, status synchronization, and various UI navigation bugs.

## [1.11.x] - 2026-02-21 - Diagnostic & Backup Hardening

- **Diagnosis Engine (v2.x)**: Added rules for Client-only mods, Corrupted JARs, DNS resolution reliability, and Geyser port conflicts.
- **Backup System (v2.1)**: Concurrency locking, unique ID generation for clusters, and smart retention logic.
- **Stability**: Rewrote remote access scripts (Caddy/Playit) with PowerShell-based integrity checks and SHA-256 binary verification.
- **Minecraft Support**: Added support for 1.21.x and legacy versions (1.7.10 to 1.19.2) with intelligent Java version pinning.
- **Hotfixes**: Resolved "ERR_REQUIRE_ESM" failures, agent-only `systeminformation` crashes, and various Bedrock 404 deployment issues.

### [1.11.0] - 2026-02-18 - Network Fabric & Systems Integrity

- **Velocity Expansion**: Full integration for high-performance proxy management, including forwarding secret synchronization and dedicated "Proxy Dynamics" UI.
- **Infrastructure Services**: New load capacity simulation, auto-scaling memory services, and CPU affinity/limits logic.
- **Cross-Play**: Native Geyser/Floodgate integration for Bedrock/Java gameplay with automated UDP port setup.
- **Systems Integrity**: Ed25519 digitally signed updates, SHA256 integrity checks, and atomic state transitions for panel upgrades.
- **Modpack Search**: Multi-source Modpack browser (Modrinth/Spiget) with advanced loader/type filtering.

## [1.10.x] - 2026-02-14 - Multi-Machine Access

- **Remote Access**: Stable multi-step wizard for Dynamic DNS (DuckDNS), Zero-Config HTTPS (Caddy), and Panic Control isolation.
- **Diagnosis (v2)**: Overhauled diagnostic engine with one-click "Auto-Fix" solutions for generic server errors.
- **Optimization**: Backend status caching for networking, image processing via `sharp` for 64x64 server icons, and high-performance log parsing.
- **Architecture**: Large-scale storage consolidation into a unified SQLite provider and a full documentation library overhaul.

## [1.10.0] - 2026-02-11 - Distributed Operations & Cluster Reliability

- **Distributed Nodes**: Automated enrollment (Bootstrap ZIP) for remote hosts with resource telemetry and spatial heatmap visualization.
- **Native Bedrock**: Automated binary repair, specialized log tracking, and world-icon customization for BDS.
- **Logic**: Embedded Monaco IDE with co-presence, bidirectional SQLite/JSON sync, and Chaos-hardened sockets.
- **UI**: Fixed navigation header, compact high-density server selection grid, and "Rainbow Hold" authentication.
- **Fixes**: Patched 10+ critical race conditions in node deployment and permission elevation checks.

## [1.9.x] - 2026-02-10 - Plugin Marketplace & Host Mode

- **Features**: Fully operational Plugin Marketplace (Modrinth/Spiget/Hangar), Host Mode master switch (Solo vs Collab), and centralized versioning via `version.json`.
- **Notifications**: Full persistent engine with Socket.IO alerts and auto-pruning.
- **Fixes**: Resolved 401 Unauthorized loops and missing UI tabs.

## [1.8.x] - 2026-02-02 - Quality Mode & Design

- **Quality Mode**: Glassmorphism, custom backgrounds, and smooth animations.
- **Adaptive UI**: Responsive grid layout with drag-and-drop persistence and Micro Mode.

## [Legacy] - Early Architecture

- **1.7.x**: Zero-Config HTTPS (Caddy), Playit.gg bridge, and 3-State Access Control.
- **1.6.x**: Pro-Grade Dashboard refresh and solidified Multi-User RBAC.
- **1.5.x**: UI Redesign and Audit Logging.
- **1.4.x**: Server Architect wiki, Atomic Writes, and Operation Locking.

## Known Issues

- **Distributed Throttling**: Docker IO (disk speed) limits remain restricted to Linux hosts due to cgroupv2 dependencies. Standard CPU/RAM isolation works across all platforms.
